Instruction: Read the following segment of an acquisition agreement and answer the corresponding multiple-choice question. The agreement states: 'Section 9.12. Superior Offer Evaluation. Notwithstanding any contradictory provisions herein, during the Pre-Closing Period, the Board may consider an offer as Superior only if it determines, in a manner compliant with its fiduciary duties and after obtaining independent assessments from its external legal counsel, financial advisor, and tax consultant, that the offer not only provides a higher financial return but also aligns with strategic, operational, and regulatory objectives. Prior to any action, the Board must issue a written Notice to the Controlling Party at least three Business Days before the effective date of any recommendation change. Furthermore, if any aspect of the offer is materially amended—be it financial terms, compliance frameworks, or operational strategies—a new assessment period shall commence.' Question: Is the 'financial point of view' the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is Superior as per this agreement? Options: A: No, B: Yes.
